{
  "name": "Kaduna",
  "description": "Kaduna is the capital of Kaduna State in northwestern Nigeria and one of the country's most important historical and commercial cities. Formerly the administrative capital of the Northern Region during colonial times, it features grand colonial buildings, wide boulevards, the Kaduna River, vibrant markets (like Central Market), and a rich multicultural heritage with Hausa, Fulani, and other ethnic influences. Known for its textile industry, educational institutions (e.g., Ahmadu Bello University nearby), and attractions like Kajuru Castle, Matsirga Waterfalls, and the National Museum, Kaduna blends history, culture, and natural beauty.",
